address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MURAKAMI KAORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKAHISA MITSUGU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI TETSUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMANAKA SUSUMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKEHATA, TOSHIHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANEDA, MASAAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MURAKAMI, KAORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKAHISA, MITSUGU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI, TETSUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMANAKA, SUSUMU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>From a metallic sheet having a circular hole (10) and laminated with a resin film (9) for a gasket, a circular sheet concentric with the circular hole (10) and larger than the circular hole is stamped. The circular sheet is then drawn into a bottomed cylinder. The cylinder is used as a case (1) with a gasket. A generating device (20) and a sealing plate (2) are placed in the case (1). The edge (2a) of the sealing plate (2) is caulked by the edge (1a) of the case (1) through the gasket (3) made of the resin and the case is sealed to produce a coin-shaped cell.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>A partir d'une feuille métallique présentant un trou circulaire (10) et stratifiée avec un film de résine (9) formant un joint d'étanchéité, on découpe une feuille circulaire, concentrique au trou circulaire (10), de diamètre supérieur à celui du trou circulaire. La feuille circulaire est ensuite étirée dans un cylindre doté d'un fond. Le cylindre est utilisé comme boîtier (1) avec joint d'étanchéité. Un dispositif générateur (20) et une plaquette d'étanchéité (2) sont placés dans le boîtier (1). Le bord (2a) de la plaquette d'étanchéité (2) est maté par le bord (1a) du boîtier (1) par le joint (3) fabriqué en résine, et le boîtier est scellé de manière à obtenir une cellule en forme de pièce de monnaie.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>